        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-19T13:45:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure what `Feature::DawnNative` means, but I don\u0027t find its usage within Chromium, and Graphite seems always use something like `wgpu::Device` ([example](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnSharedContext.h;l\u003d41)) instead of `Dawn::native::DeviceBase`?",
      "parentUuid": "08ac430b_dddc6e96",
      "revId": "9a5423b25eb5e56ed033b7be524375315547cf1a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07fd112c_abc50147",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Texture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 703,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-05T11:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I change it to a Dawn Native API of `wgpu::Texture` that can set and reset the owner GUID any time during the textures\u0027 lifecycle. In this way, we can properly set the ownership information for textures that get reused from Graphite\u0027s resource provider cache.\n\nAlso, I think with native API we can always assume we are under Native Dawn without guarding behind `Feature::DawnNative`.\n\nBy the way, I search the Dawn codebase [1] and didn\u0027t find `Feature::DawnNative` actually gating anything?\n\n[1]: https://source.chromium.org/search?q\u003d::DawnNative\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fdawn%2F",
      "parentUuid": "49249764_7a8e61da",
      "revId": "9a5423b25eb5e56ed033b7be524375315547cf1a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    }
